---
description: OCA general rules for development and revision of Odoo modules.
globs:
  - "**/*.py"
  - "**/*.xml"
alwaysApply: true
---

- Follows OCA and Odoo coding conventions.
- Use pylint-odoo and odoo-pre-commit-hooks to validate the code before committing it.
- Do not allow unnecessary imports or dead code.
- File and folder names must not contain spaces or special characters.
- Modules must have a properly defined `__manifest__.py` file.
- Models must inherit from `models.Model` and use Odoo decorators (`@api.model`, `@api.depends`, etc.) as appropriate.
- The fields must be correctly defined and documented..
- Methods must have clear and concise docstrings.
- Do not use unnecessary prints or logs in production.
- XML files must be well-formatted and comply with OCA standards.
- The translations must be in `.po` files and follow the standard structure.
- Before uploading code, run the linters and correct all reported errors.
- Do not upload external dependencies not approved by OCA.
- It follows the standard Odoo folder structure: `models`, `views`, `wizards`, `data`, `security`, etc.

